          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: étant donné que",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "étant donné que — \"given that\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Étant donné que le magasin est fermé, nous rentrons. Given that the shop is closed, we are going home."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Takes the indicative: étant donné que le magasin est fermé. Careful style, frequent in writing."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "étant donné que is built from étant, the present participle of être, and donné \"given\". donner is inherited from Latin dōnāre \"to give as a present\" (Lewis & Short)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
